## 6. Cross-Cutting Concerns

### 6.1 Security

- **API keys** (Gemini + Geoapify) live only in backend `.env` — never in frontend code.
- **Auth middleware** ensures a user can only generate itineraries for trips they own.
- **Input validation** sanitizes destination/coordinate input before it reaches third-party APIs.
- **Usage discipline**: caching (Phase 6) and category-scoped queries (Phase 7) both limit unnecessary paid API calls.

### 6.2 Performance

- Itinerary caching removes repeat Gemini calls entirely for unchanged trips.
- Nearby places are fetched **on-demand per category**, not all at once.
- `useCallback` prevents redundant re-renders of map/marker components.
- Leaflet only loads tiles for the visible viewport (standard behavior).

